  "body": "Nest and Invest!  \r\n\r\nOpportunities like this are becoming increasingly rare. Set on a substantial 653m² (more or less) freehold site in the sought-after Mixed Housing Suburban zone, this beautiful 1970s home offers the perfect blend of location and exciting future potential.\r\n\r\nMove straight in and enjoy the benefits of the location with light-filled open-plan living area capturing an elevated outlook and flows seamlessly onto a sun-soaked north-facing deck—the perfect place to unwind or entertain family and friends.\r\n\r\nThe true star of this property is the expansive backyard. With plenty of room for children and pets to play, established trees providing privacy, and ample space for gardens, outdoor entertaining or vegetable beds, it's a lifestyle that's becoming increasingly difficult to find. For buyers looking ahead, the generous land size and\r\nfavourable zoning may also offer future opportunities to explore further development or a minor dwelling (subject to council approval).\r\n\r\nAdditional features include:\r\n• 653m² (more or less) freehold section\r\n• Mixed Housing Suburban zoning\r\n• Sunny north-facing entertaining deck\r\n• Separate laundry and single garage\r\n• Walking distance to Torbay Primary School and public transport\r\n• Minutes from local shops, cafés and the beautiful East Coast beaches\r\n\r\nWhether you're searching for your first home, a family haven with room to grow, or a smart landbank investment with future upside, 66 Alexander Avenue is a property that deserves your immediate attention.  \r\n\r\nIf you're looking to buy your first home or invest in a property that has potential, this one is well worth a look.\r\n\r\nLarge freehold sites in Torbay are highly sought after. Don't miss your opportunity—call me today 022 364 5005 to arrange your viewing before someone else secures it.",
